/-!
# Coherence of a quasi-coherent module of finite type on a locally Noetherian scheme

This file proves the implication **(2) ⇒ (1)** of [Stacks, Tag 01XZ], the one direction of that
tag's equivalence that was missing: a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module of finite type on a locally
Noetherian scheme `X` is **coherent**. The content is the second field of
`SheafOfModules.IsCoherent`, namely that for every open `U`, every finite index type `I` and
every `φ : free I ⟶ F.over U`, the kernel `kernel φ` is of finite type. With it the five
conditions of the tag become equivalent and the three consequences the source draws from the
equivalence follow.

## Main results

* `isFiniteType_kernel`: the kernel condition of [Stacks, Tag 01BV] for a quasi-coherent module
  on a locally Noetherian scheme — the new mathematics of this file.
* `isCoherent_of_isQuasicoherent_isFiniteType`: **(2) ⇒ (1)** of [Stacks, Tag 01XZ].
* `coherent_tfae`: the five equivalent conditions of [Stacks, Tag 01XZ].
* `structureSheaf_isCoherent`, `isCoherent_of_isInvertible`,
  `isCoherent_of_isFiniteLocallyFree`: the three consequences drawn in the source.
* `exists_finite_generatingSections_kernel_spec`: the affine input — on the spectrum of a
  Noetherian ring, the kernel of a map from a finite free module to a quasi-coherent module is
  generated by finitely many global sections.
* `restrictEquiv`: restriction of modules along an isomorphism of schemes is an equivalence.
* `sliceEquiv`, `sliceRestrict`, `toSpec`: the transports from the slice site over `U` down to
  the spectrum of an affine open contained in `U`.
* `isFiniteType_unit`: the structure sheaf is of finite type, on an arbitrary site.
* `isFiniteType_of_coversTop`: finite generating sections over the members of a covering of the
  terminal object give finite type.

## The route

Fix `U : X.Opens`, a finite `I`, and `φ : free I ⟶ F.over U`; the kernel lives on the slice site
over `U`, so showing it of finite type means producing finite generating sections of
`(kernel φ).over W` for `W` ranging over a covering family of the slice.

1. **The cover.** `coversTop_affineSlice`: the affine opens contained in `U`, read as objects of
   `Over U`, cover the terminal object of the slice topology. This is immediate from
   `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.isBasis_affineOpens` once `GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff` and
   `Sieve.overEquiv_iff` have unwound the slice topology.

2. **Down to the spectrum.** For such a `W`, with `V := W.left` affine, `toSpec` is the composite
   of three functors: `sliceRestrict`, which restricts from the slice over `U` to the slice over
   `V` (the restriction `SheafOfModules.overFunctor` to `W` followed by the iterated-slice
   equivalence `sliceEquiv`); `Scheme.Modules.overEquiv V`, which reads a module on the slice over
   `V` as a module on the open subscheme; and restriction along `hV.isoSpec.inv`. Each factor is
   left exact — the first by `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RestrictionExact.overKernelIso`'s
   underlying `preservesFiniteLimits_overFunctor`, the other two because they are equivalences —
   and each carries the structure sheaf to the structure sheaf and preserves coproducts, so
   `kernelMapFreeIso` turns `kernel φ` into the kernel of a map
   `free I ⟶ specRestrict F hV` on `Spec Γ(X, V)`.

3. **The affine computation.** On `Spec A` with `A` Noetherian, `moduleSpecΓFunctor` is a right
   adjoint, so it carries `kernel.ι` to an injection of `Γ(kernel ζ, ⊤)` into `Γ(free I, ⊤)`;
   the latter is `I →₀ A` by `freeSectionsIso`, a finite and hence Noetherian module. So
   `Γ(kernel ζ, ⊤)` is a finite `A`-module. The kernel is quasi-coherent by
   `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QcohLimits.isQuasicoherent_kernel`, hence is the `tilde` of its
   global sections, and the `tilde` of a finite module is generated by finitely many global
   sections. This is the only step where local Noetherianity is used.

4. **Back up.** `generatingSectionsOfMap` carries generating sections backwards along each of the
   three transports, using the unit isomorphism of the first two equivalences and
   `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.restrictIsoSelf` for the third. The index type is
   unchanged throughout, so finiteness survives.

## Implementation notes

**A local instance of `PreservesColimitsOfShape`/`PreservesColimitsOfSize` is not used by
instance search here**, even when introduced by `have`, `haveI` or `letI` with the exact type
that is then requested; verified by a trace, and by the fact that the same term supplied
positionally succeeds. Every such instance is therefore named in its binder — `hcolim`, `hlim`,
`hzero`, `hcolimΨ` — and passed by name at the call sites of `mapFreeHom`, `kernelMapFreeIso`
and `generatingSectionsOfMap`.

**An instance argument whose type mentions a later implicit is synthesized too early.**
`mapFreeHom` takes `Φ` before `{I}`, and `I` is only pinned down by `φ`; writing
`mapFreeHom Φ η φ α` synthesizes `PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete ?I) Φ` while `?I` is still a
metavariable. The call sites pass `(I := I)` explicitly. For the same reason
`(hcolimΨ := inferInstance)` cannot be written inline: the instance is bound to a `have` first
and the hypothesis passed by name.

**`PreservesColimitsOfSize` for `SheafOfModules.overFunctor` does not synthesize** because
`overFunctor` is a `def` that instance search will not unfold; `isLeftAdjoint_overFunctor_slice`
supplies `Functor.IsLeftAdjoint` after a `change` to the `SheafOfModules.pushforward (𝟙 _)` it
unfolds to, and the colimit preservation then follows from the upstream instance. For the three
composites, `preservesFiniteLimits_toSpec`, `preservesZeroMorphisms_toSpec` and
`preservesColimitsOfShape_toSpec` are plain theorems whose bodies are `inferInstanceAs` on the
composite spelled out.

**`moduleSpecΓFunctor` has no `PreservesZeroMorphisms` instance** at this pin, and
`Functor.additive_of_preservesBinaryBiproducts` cannot be used to make one because it *assumes*
that class. A hand-written instance is accepted but is then not found again by instance search,
because the two `HasZeroMorphisms` instances on `(Spec A).Modules` that the declaration and the
request pick are not interchangeable at instance transparency. `PreservesKernel.iso` is therefore
avoided for it: `finite_moduleSpecΓ_kernel` uses
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QcohLimits.injective_app_kernel_ι` instead, whose conclusion is
`rfl`-equal to injectivity of `moduleSpecΓFunctor.map (kernel.ι ζ)` because taking sections over
`⊤` and restricting scalars does not change the underlying function. For the same reason
`Mono (kernel.ι ζ)`, `Zero (free I ⟶ N)` and `IsIso (Scheme.Modules.fromTildeΓ _)` are **not**
found by `infer_instance` in `(Spec A).Modules`; the last is obtained from
`AlgebraicGeometry.isQuasicoherent_iff_isIso_fromTildeΓ` and fed to `asIso` positionally.

**The iterated-slice defeq is load-bearing and holds at default transparency only.**
`sliceEquiv U W |>.functor.obj (F.over W.left)` and `(F.over U).over W` are the same sheaf —
both send `T : Over W` to `F.val.obj (op T.left.left)` — so `sliceRestrictObjIso` is literally
`((sliceEquiv U W).unitIso.app (F.over W.left)).symm`, type-ascribed at the statement so that
the check runs with no metavariables. `directSum_isQuasicoherent` (Stacks Tag 01BF) uses the
same defeq.
Likewise `sliceEquivUnitIso` and `sliceRestrictUnitIso` are `Iso.refl`.

**`SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` and the locally-free classes default their universes to `0`
under an anonymous constructor.** Every such goal here is closed by `constructor` first and the
data given after it. `isFiniteType_of_coversTop` exists for one further reason: closing the
goal `((d).generators V).IsFiniteType` for a concrete `LocalGeneratorsData d` on the slice site
exhausts the `synthInstance` budget on `HasWeakSheafify (((J.over U)).over (d.X V))`, while with
the site instances abstract the same step is immediate.

**Two copies of [Stacks, Tag 01C6] (2) exist in the repository** with identical bodies,
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree` (the tagged one) and
`Stacks.FiniteLocallyFree.IsFiniteLocallyFree` (the one with the lemmas). The statements here use
the tagged one and `isQuasicoherent_isFiniteType_of_isFiniteLocallyFree` bridges; this
duplication should be removed, not worked around twice.

No option is set and no transparency attribute is used anywhere in this file.

## What is not done

The tag carries four *distinct* comments, one per declaration, so each is its own
covering set; all four are proved here and all four attributes are attached below. The tagged statement
additionally marks its three consequences as instances. They are plain theorems here: making
`isCoherent_of_isQuasicoherent_isFiniteType` an instance would send every coherence search
recursing through quasi-coherence and finite type, and the three consequences are left to match
it rather than diverge in style. The statements are unaffected either way.

The equivalence is proved for the predicate
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.IsFiniteTildeOn` of conditions (4) and (5); no separate
statement of [Stacks, Tag 01PB] is added here — that is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentFinite.finite_sections`.

Nothing is proved about coherence on a ringed space that is not a locally Noetherian scheme, and
the devissage and Serre-type consequences of coherence are untouched.

